    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d870">

                <pb facs="1063" n="953" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg953"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11412</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornbeck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >of a Conversation With the Chinese Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >C. C. Wu</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-08">April 8, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Mr. Hornbeck said that we were all watching with interest the efforts which were
                    being made to effect the release of Mr. Bert Nelson. Dr. Wu said that he thought
                    his Government was actively endeavoring to effect this release, but that it was
                    hard to catch bandits; if military forces pressed too hard the bandits might do
                    violence to the captives; if they do not press hard enough, the bandits continue
                    to hold the captives. Mr. Hornbeck said that he hoped that the release might be
                    effected soon.</p>
                <p>Mr. Hornbeck handed the Minister a memorandum<anchor n="42" xml:id="d870-f1"/>
                    containing an account of mission property which had been forcibly occupied and
                        <pb facs="1064" n="954" xml:id="pg954"/> apparently was being appropriated
                    by Chinese in Fukien Province. He said that he hoped that the Minister would
                    give this account some thought.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">tanley</hi>] K. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Hornbeck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
